# Neox Aspire workflow

Do **not** restate or copy shared `git-flow` / `specs-before-code` packs. Use the enabled `neox-ide/neox-guidelines` plugin and the `apply-neox-guidelines` skill.

## Before non-trivial work

1. Read [`.cursor/rules/neox-rules.json`](neox-rules.json) for paths, package ids, and `specs.glossaryOwner`.
2. Ensure `specs/features/<slug>.md` exists (status ≥ `draft`).
3. Move the spec to **`defined`** before implementation; keep acceptance criteria honest (`[ ]` / `[x]`).
4. Update [`specs/README.md`](../../specs/README.md) when adding or renaming a slug.
5. Align new terms with [`specs/features/domain-glossary.md`](../../specs/features/domain-glossary.md).
6. If Shipping packages or `src/` paths change, update `neox-rules.json` `paths` and `aspire.packages` in the same change.

## Branching

Work on `feature/*` from `develop`. Do not treat `main` as day-to-day integration.
